{"abstract":"The FAA proposes to adopt a new airworthiness directive (AD) for certain MHI RJ Aviation ULC Model CL-600-2B19 (Regional Jet Series 100 & 440) airplanes; Model CL-600-2C10 (Regional Jet Series 700, 701 & 702) airplanes; Model CL-600-2C11 (Regional Jet Series 550) airplanes; Model CL-600-2D15 (Regional Jet Series 705) airplanes; Model CL-600- 2D24 (Regional Jet Series 900) airplanes; and Model CL-600-2E25 (Regional Jet Series 1000) airplanes. This proposed AD was prompted by reports of displayed headings changing from MAG to TRU with no pilot action, which may result in misleading heading information on both primary function displays (PFDs) and multi-function displays (MFDs), and misleading course information on flight management systems (FMS). This proposed AD would require amending the existing airplane flight manual (AFM) to provide the flightcrew with updated procedures for accurate heading and course information. The FAA is proposing this AD to address the unsafe condition on these products.","action":"Notice of proposed rulemaking (NPRM).","agencies":[{"id":492,"json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/492","name":"Transportation Department","parent_id":null,"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF TRANSPORTATION","slug":"transportation-department","url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/transportation-department"},{"id":159,"json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/159","name":"Federal Aviation Administration","parent_id":492,"raw_name":"Federal Aviation Administration","slug":"federal-aviation-administration","url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/federal-aviation-administration"}],"body_html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/html/2022/04/01/2022-06771.html","cfr_references":[{"chapter":null,"citation_url":null,"part":"39","title":14}],"citation":"87 FR 19026","comment_url":null,"comments_close_on":"2022-05-16","correction_of":null,"corrections":[],"dates":"The FAA must receive comments on this proposed AD by May 16, 2022.","disposition_notes":null,"docket_ids":["Docket No. FAA-2022-0155","Project Identifier MCAI-2021-00585-T"],"dockets":[{"agency_name":"FAA","documents":[{"allow_late_comments":null,"comment_count":1,"comment_end_date":"2022-05-17","comment_start_date":"2022-04-01","comment_url":"https://www.regulations.gov/commenton/FAA-2022-0155-0001","id":"FAA-2022-0155-0001","regulations_dot_gov_open_for_comment":false,"updated_at":"2023-02-28T12:20:59.154-05:00"}],"id":"FAA-2022-0155","supporting_documents":[{"document_id":"FAA-2022-0155-0002","title":"Supporting AD Document"}],"supporting_documents_count":1,"title":"MCAI-2021-00585-T MHI RJ Aviation ULC Model CL-600-2B19, CL-600-2C10, CL-600-2C11, CL-600-2D15, CL-600-2D24, and CL-600-2E25 airplanes; Airplane flight manual"}],"document_number":"2022-06771","effective_on":null,"end_page":19029,"executive_order_notes":null,"executive_order_number":null,"full_text_xml_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/xml/2022/04/01/2022-06771.xml","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2022/04/01/2022-06771/airworthiness-directives-mhi-rj-aviation-ulc-type-certificate-previously-held-by-bombardier-inc","images":{"EP01AP22.003":{"large":"https://img.federalregister.gov/EP01AP22.003/EP01AP22.003_large.png","original_size":"https://img.federalregister.gov/EP01AP22.003/EP01AP22.003_original_size.png"}},"images_metadata":{"EP01AP22.003":{"large":{"content_type":"image/png","height":516,"identifier":"EP01AP22.003","sha":"448a208f28322a48067471a48ca85451","size":42723,"url":"https://img.federalregister.gov/EP01AP22.003/EP01AP22.003_large.png","width":822},"original_size":{"content_type":"image/png","height":1106,"identifier":"EP01AP22.003","sha":"e68215bd26b373ffa122aed5d234ead0","size":27097,"url":"https://img.federalregister.gov/EP01AP22.003/EP01AP22.003_original_size.png","width":1761}}},"json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/documents/2022-06771?publication_date=